      {
        "id": "p10-q77-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that if $n$ is even, then $S(n)=\\cos\\theta$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p10-q77-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "S(n)=\\cos\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p10-q77-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Write ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "n=2k",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", remove full periods, then use the complementary and negative-angle identities.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Let $n=2k$, where $k\\in\\mathbb Z$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}S(n)&=\\sin\\left(2k\\pi+\\frac{\\pi}{2}+\\theta\\right)\\\\S(n)&=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}+\\theta\\right)\\\\S(n)&=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-(-\\theta)\\right)\\\\S(n)&=\\cos(-\\theta)\\\\S(n)&=\\cos\\theta.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q77-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Simplify $S(n)$ if $n$ is odd.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p10-q77-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "S(n)=-\\cos\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p10-q77-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Write ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "n=2k+1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", reduce by full periods, then simplify ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\sin\\left(\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Let $n=2k+1$, where $k\\in\\mathbb Z$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}S(n)&=\\sin\\left(2k\\pi+\\frac{3\\pi}{2}+\\theta\\right)\\\\S(n)&=\\sin\\left(\\theta-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)\\\\S(n)&=\\sin\\left(-\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\theta\\right)\\right)\\\\S(n)&=-\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\theta\\right)\\\\S(n)&=-\\cos\\theta.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q77-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence, write down a singular expression for $S(n)$ that shows all possible results.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p10-q77-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "S(n)=(-1)^n\\cos\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p10-q77-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "(-1)^n",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " gives the required sign for each parity.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For even $n$, $(-1)^n=1$; for odd $n$, $(-1)^n=-1$. Thus both results are expressed by\n\n$$S(n)=(-1)^n\\cos\\theta.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      }
